  "body": "## What changed\n\nThis PR adds the example case `examples/catalog/2d/slots`.\n\n- The part is a 100 x 60 x 12 mm block with two closed slots along X. Each slot is 10 mm wide, 6 mm deep and 60 mm long.\n- `Slot1` (Slot) cuts the slot at `Y15` in rows, at the levels `Z9` and `Z6`.\n- `Trochoidal slot1` (Trochoidal slot) cuts the slot at `Y-15` in 113 loops, at the full depth.\n- The two operations use the same tool (`EM-0600-4FL`), the same width and the same floor.\n- The README compares the two programs in a table and says what to look at.\n- `model/gen_slots_obj.py` writes the mesh. The geometry is original. The script checks that the mesh is watertight and that its top area is correct.\n- `docs/decisions/2861-slots-example.md` records the decisions.\n\nNo product code changes. The only Rust change is one new test with its helper in `crates/app/tests/example_catalog.rs`.\n\n## Cause\n\nThe case did not exist. The maintainer asked for a set of example cases (#2392).\n\n## The two programs\n\n| | Slot | Trochoidal slot |\n|---|---|---|\n| Motion blocks | 19 | 803 |\n| Arc blocks | 0 | 459 |\n| Cut levels | `Z9`, `Z6` | `Z6` only |\n| Cutting feed | `F600` | `F1200` |\n| Time of the feed moves | 0.60 min | 1.28 min |\n\n## Bug found\n\n#2906: a Slot wider than the tool leaves up to 0.86 mm in its round ends, and `verify` is ok. The rows touch a round end only at their end points. The README names the bug. The bug has a link on #2392.\n\nThe work found no refusal and no missing MCP parameter.\n\n## Tests\n\nPin: `slots_case_posts_a_slot_and_a_trochoidal_slot_to_the_same_floor` in `crates/app/tests/example_catalog.rs`.\n\n- Red before the case: `case 2d/slots must hold .../examples/catalog/2d/slots/slots.nc: No such file or directory`.\n- Green with the case.\n\nThe two existing catalog tests read each case folder, so they cover the new case without a change:\n\n- `every_catalog_case_opens_regenerates_verifies_and_posts_byte_for_byte`\n- `every_catalog_case_rebuilds_from_camscript`\n\nMutation results:\n\n- `build.camscript` with the Slot `stepdown` 6.0 and the committed `slots.nc`: `every_catalog_case_rebuilds_from_camscript` is red (`2d/slots: build.camscript NC differs from committed .nc`). Restored: green.\n- The case rebuilt from that script: the pin is red (`the Slot cuts two levels with a 3 mm stepdown`, left `[6.0]`, right `[9.0, 6.0]`). Restored: green.\n\nGates on the final tree:\n\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: green (`app suites: example_catalog`, 5 tests).\n- `cargo xtask catalog --check`: `checked 2d/contour-tabs`, `checked 2d/first-part`, `checked 2d/slots`.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings`: green.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone. The PR adds `slots.nc` and `slots.camproj`. It changes no existing `.nc` or `.cl` file.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- No machine ran the program.\n- The UI did not open the case in this work (`crates/ui/tests/catalog_render.rs` did not run).\n- `cargo xtask catalog --screenshots` and `--pdf` did not run.\n- No heavy lane ran. The diff adds test and example files only.\n- The leftover of #2906 is a point check of the posted tool centre path, made with a script outside the repository. The stock simulation did not measure it.\n\n## Overlaps\n\n#2883 (draft, `turning/cone-thread`) touches `crates/app/tests/example_catalog.rs`. It touches the same file, different function; whichever merges second refreshes. This PR adds its test at the end of the file.\n\nChangelog: none (an example case and its test; no product behaviour changes)\n\nEffort: medium\n\nFixes #2861\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
